From 5231ec04656d8307579107f12982a02b11f8e292 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Avery Felts <averyfelts@aol.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 17:42:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 25/27] Windows: Check code that another view of its data
 section can rewrite

Views of one data section share their pages, so a write through a writable
view changes the code FEX translated from an executable view of the same
section, without a fault or a protection change that FEX would see. The stale
translation kept running: a protector that decrypts its code into one view of
a section and runs it from another ran old code and crashed.

Wine now reports every data section view with its section handle and offset.
FEX groups views of the same section (NtCompareObjects), and code it runs from
a view whose section has another view mapped is checked against its bytes
before each instruction, as with full SMC checks, and translated again when
they changed. Code translated before a second view was mapped is dropped.
Only these views pay for the checks, and no memory is write-protected, so
system calls writing to the views work as before.
